 ## Recent releases
 
-### v1.4.0 — current stable (November 8, 2026)
+### v1.4.1 — current stable (November 9, 2026)
+
+- **Every write goes through review**: the test generation studio, Import Design, the changelog, pair programming and the Kanban quick command write on the branch of a « Generated code » card in Human Review; you read the diff, then « Create PR »
+- **A lighter left menu**: a rail of spaces with one panel at a time, « My menu » for pinned and recent pages, the Toolbox in four hubs (20 entries become 9), the 14 beta pages in a **Labo**, an offer to hide pages unused for 30 days; Ctrl+K and `/` find all 77 pages by name, group or keyword
+- **Kanban**: an « Open PR » column while a pull request waits, a « Generated by a page » filter, **Purge** of the worktrees of finished cards (a merged PR also removes its worktree and local branch)
+- **Diffs in git colours** in every theme, syntax highlighting for every stack, changed words marked, an Auto side-by-side layout and a diffstat per file
+- **First run**: the wizard sets up any AI provider (Codex, Copilot, Gemini, OpenCode, Ollama, Mistral…) and its last screen says honestly which ones are connected
+- **Multi-repo** changes run on the provider, model and effort you pick; **CI/CD Triggers** start the pipeline (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Azure Pipelines, Jenkins) when an agent opens a task's PR or the PR is merged
+- **Learning loop**: builds analysed by a model of whichever provider is selected, and the lessons now reach the spec writer and its critic too
+- **The UI charter follows the active colour theme**, Import Design, the test studio and the Visual to Code canvas included
+- **Fixes**: test generation studio runtime, the quick command with a Claude subscription and every provider, Mistral/DeepSeek/Grok outside the packaged app, deleting a server project stops its agents first, the Slack/Teams webhook URL stored encrypted, « Copy path » under WSL
+- **Security**: dependency alerts fixed (oauthlib 4.0.1, glob, minimatch, fast-uri in the bundled archify renderer)
+
+### v1.4.0 — November 8, 2026
 
 - **One UI charter**: every module (Workspace, Agents, Development, Explore, Git, Planning, Toolbox) and every Settings page in the Visual to Code style: kicker header, pill tabs with counters, cards with a coloured rail, one primary button in a bottom command bar; Settings translated and grouped by coloured theme
 - **Automatic split into small PRs**: after planning, a task over the review ceiling of its kind (100 lines for a hotfix, 200 for a bug fix or an upgrade, 300 for a refactoring, 400 for a feature, tests or docs) becomes "Part k/N" cards, one PR each; independent parts run in parallel, dependent ones stack; a merged part moves the next one on (GitHub, GitLab, Azure DevOps); one colour, mark and `groupe/<id>` label per group, on the board, the phone and the forge
